The page-speed part of the page tag (src/tracker.mjs, QY1.2) is a compact
port of @railyard/insights-web src/metrics.ts in this repository, which adapts
the page-speed collection of umami-software/umami (src/tracker/index.ts,
v3.4.0, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 Umami Software, Inc.; the full licence
text is in packages/insights-web/NOTICE).

The metric definitions (LCP, INP, CLS session windows, FCP and TTFB counted
from activation) follow GoogleChrome/web-vitals (Apache License 2.0,
Copyright Google LLC). No source file of web-vitals is copied.

Session replay (2026-10-15) vendors two prebuilt UMD bundles verbatim from
rrweb-io/rrweb (MIT License, Copyright (c) rrweb-io and contributors):
  - src/vendor/rrweb-recorder.generated.mjs <- rrweb@2.1.7 dist/rrweb.umd.min.cjs
  - src/vendor/rrweb-player.generated.mjs, rrweb-player.generated.css.mjs
    <- rrweb-player@2.1.7 dist/rrweb-player.umd.min.cjs, dist/style.min.css
Regenerate with `npm run vendor:rrweb` (scripts/vendor-rrweb.mjs) after
bumping the `rrweb` / `rrweb-player` versions in package.json. Nothing in
src/replay/ is rrweb source; it is Railyard's own ingestion, caps, storage
and dashboard code that calls the vendored recorder and player.
